    "title": "WV Board of Education votes to close, consolidate schools in 3 local counties - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joey Rather Eric Minor ,\n10 hours ago\nCHARLESTON, W.Va. (WBOY) — Following months of board meetings, votes and public debate, the West Virginia Board of Education (WVBE) officially voted to close and consolidate schools across multiple counties on Wednesday, including in Barbour, Randolph and Upshur counties.\nWith the approval, the following moves will happen:\nBarbour County Belington Middle School, Kasson Middle School and Philippi Middle School will close at the end of the 2025-2026 school year. Those students will be transferred to Philip Barbour High School’s campus. Remodel the Belington Middle School building to house Pre-K through 5th-grade students from the Junior and Belington areas starting in 2027. Randolph County At the start of the 2026-2027 school year, Harman School will close and merge its students into Jennings Randolph Elementary School, Elkins Middle School and Elkins High School. Also in 2026, North Elementary School will also close and its students will be reassigned to Jennings Randolph Elementary School. Upshur County Students at Rock Cave Elementary School will be merged into French Creek Elementary School at the end of the 2025-2026 school year. How West Virginians can access the $700 million Google settlement During Wednesday’s meeting, WVBE President Paul Hardesty said he fears more closures and consolidations are on the horizon unless the West Virginia Legislature changes the formula used to fund public schools.\n“We have to stop the bleeding and find a way to address this formula. I want to be as transparent and honest with you as I can: we have to get a legislative fix with regard to the formula or we’re going to continue having tough conversations as we’re having today,” Hardesty said.\nThe WVBE also approved closure and consolidation plans for Logan, Roane and Wetzel counties.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WBOY.com.\n4",
